    <h3>&rightarrowtail;Leader of Opposition in Rajya Sabha (1998–2004)</h3>
    <p>Singh was first elected to the upper house of Parliament, the Rajya Sabha, in 1991[37] by the legislature of the state of Assam, and was re-elected in 1995, 2001, 2007[13] and 2013.[38] From 1998 to 2004, while the Bharatiya Janata Party was in power, Singh was the Leader of the Opposition in the Rajya Sabha. In 1999, he contested for the Lok Sabha from South Delhi but was unable to win the seat in his electoral debut.[39]</p>
